historical beef between them and then people inherit this beef from their mentors and their idols.','other',702.7,747.3),(1780,80,3654,3655,'But the second type of beef is the PR beef, which is just engineered beef from PR teams to promote albums, products and collabs, which happens but isn\'t as likely because it\'s very easy to spot and it\'s quite boring because it\'s not as engaging for fans. Because you can only engage in soft topics that they both are disagreeing on, which is like someone\'s male, someone\'s female, they\'re doing similar things.','other',747.6,764.8),(1781,80,3656,3656,'Now I want to move on to four main points of rebuttal.','other',765.1,767.4),(1782,80,3657,3660,'Firstly, on to their point about how this curves with the family of the person. Firstly, I\'d like to note here that the family is likely to take a stance. They\'re probably likely to say, no, we don\'t support our son who raped this person. And if that is true, no fans will ever actually attack this person because they dissociate themselves.','other',767.7,782.1),(1783,80,3661,3662,'Secondly, it means they don\'t do this. For example, if they stay quiet or they keep supporting their son, their family member, we think it\'s quite okay for them to also receive some sort of canceling or hate from the fans because they are in fact enabling this behavior.','other',782.1,796.3),(1784,80,3663,3668,'But also, thirdly, I want to say here is that artists aren\'t even likely to attack other people from the family because this is engaging. Because if somebody only attacks someone\'s daughter, they seem winded. Why? Because why shouldn\'t you attack the artists themselves? Are they good enough? Are they such good artists you cannot point any dirt at them? You have to actually talk about your daughter and you seem weak and this doesn\'t make you a winner of this conflict.','other',796.6,819.1),(1785,80,3669,3669,'But also lastly, if it\'s something so horrible about their family, your PR team would never allow you to do this because they do assert some sort of accountability.','other',819.3,827.3),(1786,80,3670,3674,'Second thing I want to note is why these things are fake, why these things that are called out are legitimate. Because if you talk about some things without evidence, you seem weak. Fans know what stops a wording, fans stop supporting you, you lose these fans and you cannot actually win. But if it\'s something that\'s completely made up, you seem weak because you cannot actually find a reason why you are better than the other artists. Nobody wants to do this.','other',827.7,847.6),(1787,80,3675,3678,'Thirdly, under the mental harm of people and like bullying on social media when people talk about it, I just want to say that people on social media who are a type of people who go on Instagram comments and approve hate comments about each other are just a type of people who would do this on any other video. There wasn\'t like this rap or they would still like receive hate and have hate comments. This doesn\'t like change their side at all. But also they can always like get out of control by saying they stop supporting the artist.','other',847.9,873.2),(1788,80,3679,3680,'And making your point about doxxing is like simply hilarious. I have no idea how a random anonymous person from Canada who I\'m fighting with, I can suddenly know all of your information as a regular user and doxx them.','other',873.5,882.7),(1789,80,3681,3686,'And now fourthly, under last part, which is how this actually still lowers to like conflicts in like schools. For example, there have been cafeteria battles, like rap battles. I tell you that this is not, like this is, like, my diss is not a bad thing. It\'s just this is extremely easy to spot. Because if there is a rap battle inside the cafeteria, every single teacher and staff member can actually see this. These people can be detained, they can be expelled.','other',882.9,904),(1790,80,3687,3691,'Or for example, it happens on online media. There are videos of that. When people have rap battles, they\'re filmed, they will be like, it\'s very social media. It\'s very easy to spot and blame and like these people to get your repercussions. On the other hand, if this bullying will take place, for example, someone whispering like swear words to another person, it\'s very hard to prove and this person isn\'t very likely to be detained in school, which means we actually have like less bullying in school on our side.','other',904.4,926.8),(1791,80,3692,3692,'I don\'t think it\'s the only way.','other',926.9,927.7),(1792,80,3693,3693,'Yes or no, do you agree that these celebrities have a cult-like following?','poi',928.5,932.2),(1793,80,3694,3697,'A cult-like following? I think some celebrities do have a cult-like following. And I think it\'s unnecessary for every single fan to like disown their artists because there will be like a brand canceling from other people who aren\'t inherently fans. But I think the large amount of fans also are likely to call someone out because sure, they like Drake, but like firstly, they are like a woman who actually doesn\'t like support someone being a pedophile and similar things.','other',932.7,953.8),(1794,80,3698,3698,'Now I\'d like to move on to our argument here, which is on accountability.','other',954,956.9),(1795,80,3699,3700,'Okay, so firstly, I\'d like to talk about two things, capacity and intent. Let\'s talk about capacity.','other',957.5,961.8),(1796,80,3701,3709,'We tell you that these people who are artists don\'t really know a lot of things that they could like, see here, they could dig out on the other person. Why? Because they like move around same social circles. They hang out and date celebrities. For example, look at Kim K, Ariana Grande, Timothée Chalamet. They all have like a hangout with similar people. Why? Because these people can relate to them best. And if celebrities are normal people, they\'re scared that these normal people are only out for money and fame and similar things. And the implication of this is that they all the time hear things and they know secrets. This means they first hear something about a guy, then they say their friend knows something about a celebrity that they dislike, or a lot of people simply have same managers, so through them they can hear the dirt about these people.','other',962.2,997.7),(1797,80,3710,3711,'But B, even if they don\'t know the secrets at the moment, they have the capacity to find out. Because they\'re very rich, they have PR teams, they can just send someone to observe the other person and dig something up.','other',997.7,1006.5),(1798,80,3712,3714,'Now, why does incentive exclusively change on our side? Because in proposition, there isn\'t an incentive to simply call out this person once, because they\'re afraid they will be ostracized from their society. Because if you look down upon from the other celebrities, the other celebrities will think they\'re really risky, they don\'t want to talk to you, because every single celebrity has some of their secrets, and they\'re afraid that if they talk to you, all of their secrets will be out in the open, which means that people will ostracize you, and this isn\'t enough to persuade you to reveal this information.','other',1006.8,1032.7),(1799,80,3715,3719,'Now, how does this incentive exclusively change our opposition? Because these beats start to. .. and they only scale up. These are conflicts who start because of this, like the intentions for framing, but then what happens, they start small. Like for example, oh, I\'m just a better rapper than you, for example, Kendrick, who are just arguing who will be the next Michael Jackson.','other',1033,1050.5),(1800,80,3720,3720,'Then it starts like, oh, you smell your mama\'s ointment, but it escalates to people saying, oh, your girlfriend is not attractive, and over time it escalates to someone pulling out their dirty secrets, which looks like harassment, pulling out sexist jokes, some being creepy, some being physically or verbally abusive to their partners, to women generally, to staff, and similar things.','other',1050.8,1067.8),(1801,80,3721,3721,'No thank you.','other',1068.1,1068.5),(1802,80,3722,3723,'Why artists then need to escalate and actually escalate through this process is because they always want to respond harsher. Why? Two reasons. First, they don\'t want to seem weak if they stop at that point, but technically, if the feud ends at that specific moment in time, then they seem as a winner because they were the one who had a harsher blow in the end.','other',1068.6,1085.3),(1803,80,3724,3725,'So at that point, what happens is acceptable for these artists to reveal secrets because the celebrity community, no thank you, is likely to take sides when something becomes so public, which means they still keep like half of the people on their side, for example, Drake, who had DJ Khaled on their side, and KJ, who had Future on his side. Otherwise, they just really, once people see you, it\'s like risky and probably spilling, and at this point, it\'s very important to keep on this feud, to keep on winning on this huge conflict, huge conflict that could actually have people, no thank you, I\'m going to be away.','other',1085.6,1111.8),(1804,80,3726,3727,'No, they can then call them out, they can then call them out for a lot of things, and what happens is that, firstly, celebrities, when they get called out on the internet, there is huge outrage, and somebody agrees to do collabs, cycling record label sponsors stop supporting you, you lose the platform you use, for example, Kanye, the Plasta DJ, has his main sponsors, and those sponsors are the main source of money for these artists and not just some Spotify listeners, but also a lot of fans probably stop supporting you.','other',1112.3,1136.9),(1805,80,3728,3728,'The impact of this is, firstly, pretty simple, twofold, firstly, you punish those who deserve it to the fullest extent possible, because again, I have reached a lot of lawyers, they will never see the legal system actually have repercussions, the only way is to take away something that means most to them, which is fame, money, and fans, they completely deserve this, but secondly, the fans have the right to know these things,','other',1138.2,1154.7),(1806,80,3729,3730,'if a fan is listening to an artist, they have a right to know the person who they listen to, who they support, and actually enable them to prosper and profit, they need to know if that person is rapist, if they\'ve committed sexual harassment and similar things, but also practically, it means celebrities are more scared to do these things, it\'s a lower incentive to do these things, and it\'s more likely to have less sexual harassment, especially if the fan base listens to these things and actually internalizes how horrible this is, when Kendrick tells the young boys how bad it is for someone to be a rapist, they listen to this, and they\'re less likely to treat women in a likeless way, because of all of these reasons, opposition.','other',1154.9,1187.8),(1807,82,3820,3823,'And first, the word. It is hard to make, to have people be accountable when they have strong PR teams behind them. Then when they have PR teams, they\'re going to make a deal, make nothing go out public, and actually not get any benefits of people calling you out. And rich artists who just pay a small fine to another artist for them to not call you out is just to make it happen that they will not get the accountability that we need on our side.','other',1870.5,1901),(1808,82,3824,3824,'In my speech, I\'m gonna go through, like, three extreme points of rebuttal in my third argument about engineered PR teams.','other',1901.1,1906.4),(1809,82,3825,3825,'So first, let\'s talk about accountability of celebrities.','other',1906.7,1909.3),(1810,82,3826,3837,'First, I want to tackle their point how there\'s gonna be mostly fake or lying. We 