ext\": \"foreign reserves to equal 100% of money\", \"start\": 252.0, \"duration\": 5.44}, {\"text\": \"in circulation. This allows Pima to sell\", \"start\": 254.48, \"duration\": 5.599}, {\"text\": \"US dollars and buyas to stabilize the\", \"start\": 257.44, \"duration\": 5.44}, {\"text\": \"currency, effectively increasing demand.\", \"start\": 260.079, \"duration\": 4.801}, {\"text\": \"Moving on, then our first argument about\", \"start\": 262.88, \"duration\": 3.68}, {\"text\": \"economic growth led by increased\", \"start\": 264.88, \"duration\": 3.759}, {\"text\": \"international revenue. First on why the\", \"start\": 266.56, \"duration\": 4.639}, {\"text\": \"USD rate is so high. The dollar is used\", \"start\": 268.639, \"duration\": 4.641}, {\"text\": \"by many as the world\'s reserve currency.\", \"start\": 271.199, \"duration\": 3.28}, {\"text\": \"Countries around the world have\", \"start\": 273.28, \"duration\": 2.88}, {\"text\": \"literally trillions in US dollar\", \"start\": 274.479, \"duration\": 3.44}, {\"text\": \"reserves, increasing demand at its\", \"start\": 276.16, \"duration\": 4.319}, {\"text\": \"value. Second, why a harmless flow of\", \"start\": 277.919, \"duration\": 5.201}, {\"text\": \"foreign money into Panama. A strong USD\", \"start\": 280.479, \"duration\": 4.241}, {\"text\": \"makes Panameanian exports more\", \"start\": 283.12, \"duration\": 3.519}, {\"text\": \"expensive, hurting its competitiveness\", \"start\": 284.72, \"duration\": 3.759}, {\"text\": \"against countries with lower currencies\", \"start\": 286.639, \"duration\": 4.161}, {\"text\": \"such as Mexico or Vietnam. It also\", \"start\": 288.479, \"duration\": 4.641}, {\"text\": \"disencourages in foreign investment and\", \"start\": 290.8, \"duration\": 5.2}, {\"text\": \"tourism as businesses face higher costs.\", \"start\": 293.12, \"duration\": 5.04}, {\"text\": \"Third, on why foreign influx of money is\", \"start\": 296.0, \"duration\": 4.639}, {\"text\": \"crucial for growth. Exports make up half\", \"start\": 298.16, \"duration\": 5.039}, {\"text\": \"of Panama\'s overall economy. Tourism and\", \"start\": 300.639, \"duration\": 5.361}, {\"text\": \"services account for 80% of its GDP.\", \"start\": 303.199, \"duration\": 4.321}, {\"text\": \"Increasing those will dramatically\", \"start\": 306.0, \"duration\": 3.759}, {\"text\": \"increase revenue. Crucially, Panama is\", \"start\": 307.52, \"duration\": 4.32}, {\"text\": \"an ideal place for investors. Its canal\", \"start\": 309.759, \"duration\": 4.0}, {\"text\": \"access reduces transportation cost\", \"start\": 311.84, \"duration\": 3.6}, {\"text\": \"drastically. It has a high rate of\", \"start\": 313.759, \"duration\": 4.0}, {\"text\": \"unemployment population that makes cheap\", \"start\": 315.44, \"duration\": 4.08}, {\"text\": \"labor potential. And with the US trying\", \"start\": 317.759, \"duration\": 3.761}, {\"text\": \"to divert its imports from China, it is\", \"start\": 319.52, \"duration\": 3.2}, {\"text\": \"looking for new locations for\", \"start\": 321.52, \"duration\": 3.92}, {\"text\": \"manufacturing. The only reason Panama\'s\", \"start\": 322.72, \"duration\": 4.88}, {\"text\": \"economy has been stagnant so far is the\", \"start\": 325.44, \"duration\": 4.56}, {\"text\": \"overpriced currency making them lose to\", \"start\": 327.6, \"duration\": 4.64}, {\"text\": \"competitors. The implication is that our\", \"start\": 330.0, \"duration\": 4.479}, {\"text\": \"policy doesn\'t only help sell existing\", \"start\": 332.24, \"duration\": 4.799}, {\"text\": \"exports but attract MNC\'s to create new\", \"start\": 334.479, \"duration\": 4.56}, {\"text\": \"ones kicking forward the manufacturing\", \"start\": 337.039, \"duration\": 4.321}, {\"text\": \"industry that is only 5% of the economy\", \"start\": 339.039, \"duration\": 4.88}, {\"text\": \"right now. Finally on the impacts\", \"start\": 341.36, \"duration\": 4.88}, {\"text\": \"firstly growth translates into increased\", \"start\": 343.919, \"duration\": 4.641}, {\"text\": \"revenue from tax collection. This allows\", \"start\": 346.24, \"duration\": 4.08}, {\"text\": \"the public sector to grow and provide\", \"start\": 348.56, \"duration\": 3.84}, {\"text\": \"people with better welfare, education\", \"start\": 350.32, \"duration\": 4.24}, {\"text\": \"and policy. It allows the government to\", \"start\": 352.4, \"duration\": 4.32}, {\"text\": \"pay its grippling debt. It creates a\", \"start\": 354.56, \"duration\": 4.72}, {\"text\": \"fiscal solution for economic crisis.\", \"start\": 356.72, \"duration\": 5.12}, {\"text\": \"Secondly, it diversifies the economy.\", \"start\": 359.28, \"duration\": 4.88}, {\"text\": \"This diversification is crucial. It\", \"start\": 361.84, \"duration\": 4.24}, {\"text\": \"makes Panama more self-sufficient and\", \"start\": 364.16, \"duration\": 4.0}, {\"text\": \"less reliant on imports in the long run,\", \"start\": 366.08, \"duration\": 3.52}, {\"text\": \"thus making it less vulnerable to\", \"start\": 368.16, \"duration\": 3.039}, {\"text\": \"tariffs and economic pressure from the\", \"start\": 369.6, \"duration\": 3.68}, {\"text\": \"US. It prevents economic shocks that\", \"start\": 371.199, \"duration\": 4.0}, {\"text\": \"impact one industry to drag down the\", \"start\": 373.28, \"duration\": 4.08}, {\"text\": \"entire economy. It creates more diverse\", \"start\": 375.199, \"duration\": 4.161}, {\"text\": \"job options with manufacturing jobs\", \"start\": 377.36, \"duration\": 3.679}, {\"text\": \"being more accessible to the poor and\", \"start\": 379.36, \"duration\": 4.16}, {\"text\": \"uneducated. It creates a virtuous cycle.\", \"start\": 381.039, \"duration\": 4.241}, {\"text\": \"revenue from manufacturing exports can\", \"start\": 383.52, \"duration\": 4.32}, {\"text\": \"be reinvested in machinery and R&D that\", \"start\": 385.28, \"duration\": 4.56}, {\"text\": \"improves manufacturing productivity and\", \"start\": 387.84, \"duration\": 4.16}, {\"text\": \"creates even more growth. You can\'t\", \"start\": 389.84, \"duration\": 4.24}, {\"text\": \"improve the productivity of services and\", \"start\": 392.0, \"duration\": 3.759}, {\"text\": \"technology. So when off there\'s a\", \"start\": 394.08, \"duration\": 3.92}, {\"text\": \"ceiling to growth. Moving on then to our\", \"start\": 395.759, \"duration\": 4.801}, {\"text\": \"second argument about crisis. First we\", \"start\": 398.0, \"duration\": 4.0}, {\"text\": \"think that the control of monetary\", \"start\": 400.56, \"duration\": 3.44}, {\"text\": \"policy is crucial for response to\", \"start\": 402.0, \"duration\": 4.88}, {\"text\": \"economic crisis. During COVID, Tano\'s\", \"start\": 404.0, \"duration\": 6.08}, {\"text\": \"debt increased from 40% to GD uh 40% of\", \"start\": 406.88, \"duration\": 7.12}, {\"text\": \"GDP to 63% and its economy shrank 18%.\", \"start\": 410.08, \"duration\": 5.76}, {\"text\": \"This is nearly double of what other\", \"start\": 414.0, \"duration\": 3.44}, {\"text\": \"countries with monetary policy\", \"start\": 415.84, \"duration\": 4.16}, {\"text\": \"experience. All because Panama only had\", \"start\": 417.44, \"duration\": 4.879}, {\"text\": \"fiscal tools. So why is that bad?\", \"start\": 420.0, \"duration\": 4.88}, {\"text\": \"Firstly, legislative processes to decide\", \"start\": 422.319, \"duration\": 5.121}, {\"text\": \"fiscal policies were too slow. A bill\", \"start\": 424.88, \"duration\": 4.159}, {\"text\": \"needs to be written, open for public\", \"start\": 427.44, \"duration\": 3.28}, {\"text\": \"comments, debated in parliament,\", \"start\": 429.039, \"duration\": 3.761}, {\"text\": \"amended, and voted on. This process\", \"start\": 430.72, \"duration\": 4.4}, {\"text\": \"takes months. This means at best the\", \"start\": 432.8, \"duration\": 4.72}, {\"text\": \"crisis tracks longer. At worst, by the\", \"start\": 435.12, \"duration\": 4.32}, {\"text\": \"time you pass a bill, it is too late to\", \"start\": 437.52, \"duration\": 4.16}, {\"text\": \"solve it. On our side, the central bank\", \"start\": 439.44, \"duration\": 4.08}, {\"text\": \"can respond promptly with monetary\", \"start\": 441.68, \"duration\": 4.32}, {\"text\": \"stimulus like lowering interest rates.\", \"start\": 443.52, \"duration\": 4.799}, {\"text\": \"Secondly, fiscal solutions accumulate\", \"start\": 446.0, \"duration\": 4.319}, {\"text\": \"debt. When your only way to create\", \"start\": 448.319, \"duration\": 4.16}, {\"text\": \"stimulus is to increase spending in a\", \"start\": 450.319, \"duration\": 4.081}, {\"text\": \"time when there is less productivity and\", \"start\": 452.479, \"duration\": 4.241}, {\"text\": \"revenue. Your only option is to borrow\", \"start\": 454.4, \"duration\": 4.4}, {\"text\": \"money. With monetary independence, you\", \"start\": 456.72, \"duration\": 3.759}, {\"text\": \"can create stimulus without a debt\", \"start\": 458.8, \"duration\": 4.239}, {\"text\": \"crisis via interest rate reforms. money,\", \"start\": 460.479, \"duration\": 5.041}, {\"text\": \"money creation or quantitative easing.\", \"start\": 463.039, \"duration\": 4.56}, {\"text\": \"Thirdly, fiscal solutions are too\", \"start\": 465.52, \"duration\": 4.239}, {\"text\": \"politicized because fiscal solutions\", \"start\": 467.599, \"duration\": 3.6}, {\"text\": \"need to be passed in parliament.\", \"start\": 469.759, \"duration\": 3.601}, {\"text\": \"Political incentives spies them. This\", \"start\": 471.199, \"duration\": 3.68}, {\"text\": \"looks like adoption of irres\", \"start\": 473.36, \"duration\": 3.76}, {\"text\": \"irresponsible and populistic solutions.\", \"start\": 474.879, \"duration\": 4.0}, {\"text\": \"This means no solutions to inflation\", \"start\": 477.12, \"duration\": 3.519}, {\"text\": \"crisis as fiscally holding the market\", \"start\": 478.879, \"duration\": 3.281}, {\"text\": \"can only happen through cutting\", \"start\": 480.639, \"duration\": 3.361}, {\"text\": \"government spending which is extremely\", \"start\": 482.16, \"duration\": 4.08}, {\"text\": \"unpopular. On our side, the politically\", \"start\": 484.0, \"duration\": 4.08}, {\"text\": \"independent central bank can design a\", \"start\": 486.24, \"duration\": 3.519}, {\"text\": \"responsible solution that will reduce\", \"start\": 488.08, \"duration\": 4.08}, {\"text\": \"the public pressure on government.\", \"start\": 489.759, \"duration\": 5.041}, {\"text\": \"Second on why the Fed won\'t save time.\", \"start\": 492.16, \"duration\": 4.159}, {\"text\": \"Firstly, the Fed will only resolve an\", \"start\": 494.8, \"duration\": 3.119}, {\"text\": \"economic crisis that hits the US\", \"start\": 496.319, \"duration\": 3.921}, {\"text\": \"directly. An economic crisis in Panama\", \"start\": 497.919, \"duration\": 4.0}, {\"text\": \"doesn\'t always mean an economic crisis\", \"start\": 500.24, \"duration\": 4.16}, {\"text\": \"in the US. Since the US has a much more\", \"start\": 501.919, \"duration\": 4.241}, {\"text\": \"diverse and wealthy economy, they\'re\", \"start\": 504.4, \"duration\": 3.44}, {\"text\": \"less likely to be hit with concerned\", \"start\": 506.16, \"duration\": 4.24}, {\"text\": \"crisis. Secondly, even when a crisis\", \"start\": 507.84, \"duration\": 4.48}, {\"text\": \"does hit both countries, the Fed will\", \"start\": 510.4, \"duration\": 3.92}, {\"text\": \"intervene in ways that only benefit the\", \"start\": 512.32, \"duration\": 4.32}, {\"text\": \"US, not Panama. Firstly, because\", \"start\": 514.32, \"duration\": 4.48}, {\"text\": \"American interests favor prioritizing\", \"start\": 516.64, \"duration\": 4.24}, {\"text\": \"price stability at the expense of growth\", \"start\": 518.8, \"duration\": 4.4}, {\"text\": \"and unemployment, the American economy\", \"start\": 520.88, \"duration\": 4.56}, {\"text\": \"is high-tech and refining based. It buys\", \"start\": 523.2, \"duration\": 3.68}, {\"text\": \"raw materials and then refineses them\", \"start\": 525.44, \"duration\": 3.28}, {\"text\": \"into high quality products. Which means\", \"start\": 526.88, \"duration\": 3.76}, {\"text\": \"that when prices increase, it doesn\'t\", \"start\": 528.72, \"duration\": 3.84}, {\"text\": \"only increase American cost of living,\", \"start\": 530.64, \"duration\": 4.0}, {\"text\": \"but also cost of production, resulting\", \"start\": 532.56, \"duration\": 4.24}, {\"text\": \"in business collapse and job loss. In\", \"start\": 534.64, \"duration\": 4.16}, {\"text\": \"contrast, more developing economies are\", \"start\": 536.8, \"duration\": 3.84}, {\"text\": \"not as vulnerable to price increases.\", \"start\": 538.8, \"duration\": 3.36}, {\"text\": \"They are much more vulnerable to\", \"start\": 540.64, \"duration\": 3.759}, {\"text\": \"stagnation as it makes them struggle to\", \"start\": 542.16, \"duration\": 3.76}, {\"text\": \"keep their underdeveloped industries\", \"start\": 544.399, \"duration\": 3.761}, {\"text\": \"afloat. This is why in the current\", \"start\": 545.92, \"duration\": 4.479}, {\"text\": \"economic crisis, the Fed has been very\", \"start\": 548.16, \"duration\": 4.0}, {\"text\": \"reluctant to reduce interest rates.\", \"start\": 550.399, \"duration\": 3.361}, {\"text\": \"While in countries like India, the\", \"start\": 552.16, \"duration\": 3.28}, {\"text\": \"central bank has already lowered\", \"start\": 553.76, \"duration\": 3.68}, {\"text\": \"interest rates several times. Panama\'s\", \"start\": 555.44, \"duration\": 3.839}, {\"text\": \"economy is much more similar to India\'s\", \"start\": 557.44, \"duration\": 4.079}, {\"text\": \"than the US. Yet, its response to crisis\", \"start\": 559.279, \"duration\": 4.961}, {\"text\": \"is tied to the Fed. Secondly, the Fed\", \"start\": 561.519, \"duration\": 4.561}, {\"text\": \"also tailored its policy to