INSERT INTO `rounds` VALUES (5,'WSDC 2025 R5 - Portugal vs Japan','2026-02-14 21:59:31',1,'external_video',NULL,'wsdc','THS the Holy See recognizing the underground Catholic church in China, rather than the government-sanctioned church.','Religion, Human rights','X0WrhIO6O-w','public','{\"task\": \"transcribe\", \"text\": \"My name is Shiga, I\'m trying to teach. Shiga, for now, please address the panel as a whole. I\'ll let the panelists introduce themselves and then we can get started. I encourage you all to keep your own time. There should be a time cap at the board, but just in case, use your cell phones. I\'m Travis, I\'ll be a panelist for the surrounding budget. I\'m Phil, teaching in my English course, thank you for asking. Okay, so for the two first propositions. Panel, the Holy See signed an agreement with an ultra-orthodox state that persecutes religious minorities. This agreement guaranteed that a point of issue is not an incitement to regime and close your eyes to the persecution of their Catholic brothers and sisters. This agreement was signed in 1933 with the Nazi Germany. We should not make the same mistakes and we should learn from the past. So how did you propose? What I\'ll do in this speech. First of all, I\'ll explain why I made this argument. I\'m trying to recognize the University of Chicago Church in China and my failure to do so makes it completely authoritarian persecution. Before I make those arguments, a few pieces of setup. What was the cause of neutrality for the last years? History is not tied to neutrality in the face of opposition. When the Vatican signed an agreement with the Nazi regime in hopes to secure religious freedom, instead it lent authority to tyranny. With the same state being held now repeatedly against it in China. Since 2018, the Vatican entered a secret agreement with the Chinese Communist Party. It handed the right to a point of issue to a government that subdues churches, jails, prisons, and places a gruesomely close focus of their present Xi Jinping. That agreement has led to no real gains. Underdog Catholics remain persecuted. State churches preach the law to the party, not to God. And what has the Vatican done? We must understand the intentional localization of religion by the Chinese Communist Party and Xi Jinping. Since early 2000s, and especially under Xi, the regime has launched a systematic policy called socialization. A campaign to conserve all religious tools of the state, strip the form and influence, and align with the Communist ideology. What does this mean in practice? It means, for example, religious texts are removed to reflect party values. Images of Jesus are being replaced by proteins. Servants are monitored, punished, and imprisoned if they resist. And so on and so forth. This Communist regime, also the same regime that imprisons over 1 million people Muslims in re-education camps, vandalizes the beaten Buddhist practice, and persecutes fellow non-followers to the point of forced war on their hearts. Furthermore, the state church is not an independent religious institution. It is an extension of state repression. The Vatican in 1957 by-law was drawn and by the party to fracture the Catholic Church and co-opt its spiritual influence. So when the Vatican recognizes the state church, it is not protecting faith. It is endorsing a lie, a fabricated church built to silence dissent and legitimize dictatorship. This debate asks, will the Holy See stand with the machinery of tyrants that rewrites the gospel and buries the martyrs in silence, or with those who, like the Christian pentecostal, chose faith over fear, Christ over Caesar? So, moving on to our first argument, on how the Holy See has a moral duty to its followers. The first reason why. The Holy See has a duty to the Catholics as the one who inherits the world\'s religious spirit, founder of the Catholic Church. Therefore, being the only institution capable of providing a legitimate synodality to all the members of the clergy, with the pope being the direct representative of God\'s will of martyrdom. That means that a Catholic can direct the Holy See to be able to exercise their faith, a core of their identities. So, a canonical canonist can only be baptized, for example, if the atheist is a willful and a member of the clergy, or the sacred writes false news, and that false canon never attains the artist, for example, and all the others need the Vatican to be able to exercise their religion. Therefore, the false autonomy and capability of self-automization, of fulfilling their metaphysical needs, of achieving salvation and avoiding eternal punishment in the afterlife, is only possible if the Holy See, through its actions of representatives, recognizes and endorses their faith. That creates a strong moral obligation of the Holy See, since it is the only entity responsible and capable of enabling their multidecimal autonomy to the Christians. Second reason. Condoning and actively recognizing an oppressive regime such as the Chinese regime, even with the aim of minimizing its harms, is tenuous and helpful for two main reasons. Eighth. To recognize it is to grant legitimacy to the regime and consequently to its actions. It is a symbolic act of empowerment and support for a blood-same state. There is no way to separate these actions. Supporting one facet of the regime is supported with success and consolidation, which means being completely disenfranchised. If you make any kind of agreement, this means you\'re giving some kind of legitimacy and giving legitimacy to all actions, but only to one party. Second. The recognition also implies approval of the moral morality of the regime\'s actions and its underlying values. It is the establishment of certain tactics as officially accepted, such as attacks on freedom of expression by the government and attacks on freedom of religion, the destruction of human dignity through torture, rape, imprisonment, authoritarianism, and disre