sive humanitarian losses.',115525,115532),(6317,8,'It was literally gunning down protesters.',115533,115538),(6318,8,'Even if it led to success at the end, the youth aren\'t tired of continuing to engage in future protests.',115539,115558),(6319,8,'So there isn\'t a substantial risk of a protest.',115559,115567),(6320,8,'What this means is, young people will struggle to turn up to vote, and the BNP\'s political power is likely to be entrenched, because when it is in power, it will continue gaining access to funding by being in power and by being the incumbent party, meaning future political competition is unlikely to threaten it.',115568,115622),(6321,8,'No, thank you.',115623,115625),(6322,8,'Third, the BNP\'s existing voter block is much less fractured.',115626,115635),(6323,8,'Historically, people who are worried about Indian infrastructure in Bangladesh\'s politics are people with more of an Islamist name have sided with the BNP, and their voter block is unlikely to fracture in the future, meaning other political parties will simply be absorbed by the power of the BNP.',115636,115684),(6324,8,'As a consequence, the BNP is unlikely to face large political competition, and in their best case, the coup does not happen.',115685,115706),(6325,8,'Why does this matter?',115707,115710),(6326,8,'Because the BNP is, first, because at least all the PM\'s arguments on political competition are wrong.',115711,115727),(6327,8,'Political competition is symmetric.',115728,115731),(6328,8,'But second, then you listen to the BNP\'s arguments on young people and why the BNP will cater to them.',115732,115751),(6329,8,'First, the BNP will not cater to them.',115752,115759),(6330,8,'What are their arguments here?',115760,115764),(6331,8,'One, they say youth voters are energized for the protests.',115765,115774),(6332,8,'This is an assertion.',115775,115778),(6333,8,'I\'ve demonstrated the substantial exhaustion among youth voters after the protests, combined with complacency about B