025),(6437,8,'It is harder to cut down on civil society figures because they\'re perceived as less than equal because it\'s opposed by international actors.',118026,118048),(6438,8,'Which means it\'s important to seize your notoriety to be in these civil society figures.',118049,118063),(6439,8,'A place where it\'s important to have powerful individuals, weakening politics is probably already covered by individuals being motivated to vote, caring about politics in a historically unique way.',118064,118092),(6440,8,'I\'m going to just read the speech so I can get my bag.',118093,118105),(6441,8,'Or if anything, I can come back in time to read it.',118106,118117),(6442,8,'What if I get my bag? Never mind.',118118,118125),(6443,8,'We thank the speaker very much for their speech and we now welcome the member of opposition.',118126,118142),(6444,8,'Firstly on the future political system of Bangladesh.',118143,118150),(6445,8,'Secondly on stability and why the BNP would be bad for it as well as incredibly bad governments.',118151,118168),(6446,8,'Let\'s start with the future political system of Bangladesh.',118169,118177),(6447,8,'Because we think the biggest of the fault in this debate isn\'t about who wins government the next time.',118178,118196),(6448,8,'Because what\'s happening at the moment is we have an interim government and before we go to another general election, they\'re going to have an election before that to form the special assembly to rewrite the Bangladeshi constitution and reform the government institutions of that country.',118197,118242),(6449,8,'And the most important thing in this debate is who has power in that to form the long term constitution of Bangladesh, what the formation of government is going to look like.',118243,118274),(6450,8,'And that very intuitively outweighs the rest of the debate.',118275,118284),(6451,8,'So they\'re talking about all of the government structures that inform every single election into the future.',118285,118301),(6452,8,'What are the problems with Bangladesh\'s political system at the moment?',118302,118312),(6453,8,'First of all, the massive rigging of elections.',118313,118320),(6454,8,'What was supposed to happen is that the government prior to an election would give up power to a caretaker government such that they weren\'t in power during that election so that they couldn\'t rig it.',118321,118356),(6455,8,'The Awami League refused to do that and that\'s why the BNP boycotted almost every election in the last decade.',118357,118376),(6456,8,'So, secondly, there\'s an enormous amount of corruption in Bangladesh\'s government.',118377,118387),(6457,8,'That\'s to say there\'s an enormous amount of embezzlement, an enormous amount of people who are appointed bureaucrats who continue to preserve their own image.',118388,118412),(6458,8,'There\'s also an enormous amount of judicial problems.',118413,118420),(6459,8,'Judicial actors, members of the judiciary essentially act in line with political parties.',118421,118433),(6460,8,'All of them were supposed to mass resign in protest because they were trying to bring back Shere Khasana after she had fled to India.',118434,118458),(6461,8,'There\'s an enormous amount of problems that need to be solved in this constitutional assembly.',118459,118473),(6462,8,'And currently, the interim government has established a large number of commissions under Mohammed Hassan and also with the involvement of the student leaders to reform these policies.',118474,118501),(6463,8,'Why is it dead?',118502,118505),(6464,8,'Yeah, Yunus has a notable primacy.',118506,118511),(6465,8,'Do you think that the international actors are likely to run and rotate within or are you averse to this trend?',118512,118532),(6466,8,'Hassan is in general running the next election.',118533,118540),(6467,8,'We believe he\'s turning a caretaker, which is what he did in the last caretaker election about 20 years ago.',118541,118560),(6468,8,'He\'s very explicitly a caretaker.',118561,118565),(6469,8,'He\'s not here to be a long-term political actor in Bangladesh.',118566,118577),(6470,8,'So, why is it that it is necessary to have these people involved in the constitutional assembly?',118578,118594),(6471,8,'First of all, the existing forces in politics benefited from each of these systems.',118595,118608),(6472,8,'All of their allies, they were put in place by the existing political system.',118609,118622),(6473,8,'So they\'re incredibly unlikely to want to change it.',118623,118631),(6474,8,'But secondly, without a force, without a specifically large institutional force against this, it\'s likely that any smaller forces that OG talks about, like individuals or small groups of two or three running, would be able to get this change through.',118632,118672),(6475,8,'They\'re likely to be bought off or horse-traded by the larger parties.',118673,118685),(6476,8,'They\'re less likely to have an agreement on what this reform should look like.',118686,118699),(6477,8,'So even if they all agree there should be reform, if they don\'t agree on it, they\'re on net and are going to get outvoted.',118700,118724),(6478,8,'And also, they weren\'t involved in the creation of it.',118725,118734),(6479,8,'The student leaders got Mohammed Hassan in.',118735,118741),(6480,8,'They served in roles with those commissions developing it.',118742,118750),(6481,8,'So, they are the ones who are involved in the development and can get it passed through.',118751,118767),(6482,8,'Why is it that they can only get this done if they are a party?',118768,118782),(6483,8,'First of all, being a part of a party is necessary for branding and selling your candidate.',118783,118799),(6484,8,'And secondly, elections are big business.',118800,118805),(6485,8,'You need operatives, you need money, you need ads, you need institutional capacity.',118806,118818),(6486,8,'You can\'t do this with two or three individuals.',118819,118827),(6487,8,'The next thing I want to prove is that other institutional power in Bangladesh is very, very rare.',118828,118845),(6488,8,'Because they can always go to other institutions where you might support.',118846,118857),(6489,8,'But there\'s good structural reasons to believe there aren\'t a lot of other large institutions in Bangladesh that can form themselves into political parties.',118858,118881),(6490,8,'First of all, it\'s an authoritarian country.',118882,118888),(6491,8,'Secondly, the Oman, which meant that they were going to shut down any alternative institutional power base.',118889,118905),(6492,8,'Secondly, the Omani League tried to position itself as a big tent party that could include anyone in.',118906,118923),(6493,8,'So, they had an incentive to try and bring in any other institutions and align themselves with the Omani League.',118924,118943),(6494,8,'And thirdly, Bangladesh has been in chaos for many years.',118944,118953),(6495,8,'The initial protest against the quota system started in 2018.',118954,118963),(6496,8,'And in that context of chaos, it\'s very difficult to form institutional power.',118964,118976),(6497,8,'So, that means that there aren\'t a lot of other large institutions that could step into this gap.',118977,118994),(6498,8,'The best comparison then is the BNP or other smaller parties.',118995,119005),(6499,8,'Open government always says, well, students are seen as bad, they\'re seen as irrational, they\'re seen as too young.',119006,119024),(6500,8,'But the problem with this is that this party isn\'t just going to run students.',119025,119039),(6501,8,'They\'re going to bring other people in.',119040,119046),(6502,8,'For instance, they brought in Hassan in the short run.',119047,119056),(6503,8,'Also, they brought in a large number of university professors who actually designed the original system of reform.',119057,119074),(6504,8,'They worked with their own professors.',119075,119080),(6505,8,'And military leaders, as Open Opposition points out, military leaders who told the military to put down their arms, not to oppose this.',119081,119103),(6506,8,'And those people have almost nothing in common, except for the fact that they were brought together by an anti-discrimination student movement.',119104,119126),(6507,8,'That is why they\'re likely to be taken seriously.',119127,119135),(6508,8,'And they\'re also robots closing government, because, like, well, they\'re incredibly terrible.',119136,119147),(6509,8,'But they brought in a large amount of support.',119148,119156),(6510,8,'The key thing is that they are important for bringing those people together.',119157,119169),(6511,8,'But I also want to note here, not only is it important that they\'re part of the Constitutional Assembly to solve all those problems, but it\'s also important that they are the first government afterwards.',119170,119204),(6512,8,'Because as I allude to, the entire Supreme Court of Bangladesh was forced to resign because they were seen as trying to bring back Sheikh Hasani.',119205,119230),(6513,8,'That means that they\'re going to get to appoint the next set of justices who will make the first interpretations of the new Constitution that will serve as the baseline precedent against which that Constitution is interpreted.',119231,119267),(6514,8,'And that\'s incredibly important.',119268,119271),(6515,8,'They also set the norms of how it\'s interpreted.',119272,119280),(6516,8,'And if another party wins, they have incentive to show that the new rules that they don\'t like are very bad and very difficult in order to manufacture consent to get them taken away.',119281,119314),(6517,8,'It\'s very important that they are not only involved in the right to do it, but that they are the first party to interpret it and to appoint the justices who do so.',119315,119347),(6518,8,'What are the benefits of this?',119348,119353),(6519,8,'It means that you get a government that functions, which is important for your economics.',119354,119368),(6520,8,'It also means you get rid of the quota system, which is not only un-democratic, but also incredibly bad for the functioning of government, because you appoint a large number of freedom fighters to the system, not because they\'re good.',119369,119409),(6521,8,'And it makes, and crucially, it makes the Bangladesh Public Service not politically neutral, because the freedom fighters that are appointed have political allegiances.',119410,119433),(6522,8,'And it means you don\'t have a neutral public service.',119434,119443),(6523,8,'That pretty much weighs pretty intuitively over the rest of the debate. Second extension.',119444,119457),(6524,8,'Why is it that you get more stability?',119458,119465),(6525,8,'Opening government says you get the military coup.',119466,119473),(6526,8,'Opening office pretty astutely points out that the military can explicitly allow a moment to come through.',119474,119490),(6527,8,'You\'re very unlikely to get the military coup.',119491,119498),(6528,8,'Why is it that the BNP would be incredibly bad at this ability?',119499,119511),(6529,8,'First of all, their leader is not somebody who can legitimately run, he\'s been charged with anti-corruption, and different courts have split over his actual legitimacy as a candidate.',119512,119541),(6530,8,'So, that means that they\'re incredibly likely to be protested.',119542,119551),(6531,8,'Secondly, there\'s very likely to be hindered protests, where this aggressively pro-Muslim party wins, who have done terrible things to women and minorities in the past.',119552,119578),(6532,8,'And thirdly, your relationship with India is likely to be substantially worse, and they\'re likely to foment unrest on the ground.',119579,119599),(6533,8,'We already saw Indian forces in the country protecting Sheikh Hasana on her side during the last revolution, and they have an intention to foment chaos in the country in order to re-establish their influence.',119600,119635),(6534,8,'And I know these aren\'t the only reasons why you don\'t get stability.',119636,119648),(6535,8,'There are also reasons why the BNP is bad.',119649,119657),(6536,8,'Like, they are anti-Hindu, we should care about Hindu.',119658,119667),(6537,8,'They are anti-India, we should care about your relationship with India, your trade relationship, your security relationship.',119668,119685),(6538,8,'They have done corruption, which is not only that you can\'t legitimately run, but also, you know, corruption is bad.',119686,119705),(6539,8,'Additionally, I think it\'s important that these student leaders are there to be able to tamp down protests.',119706,119723),(6540,8,'Open Opposition says, well, student leaders might do protest, but I think that\'s the lower impact argument, because their protests are naturally pretty good and pretty reasonable.',119724,119750),(6541,8,'What\'s more important is the bad, more aggressive sets of protests that might come from other actors, which we think they\'re uniquely good at tamping down and stopping the Indian violence.',119751,119781),(6542,8,'First of all, people are going to feel lied to if these people don\'t follow through on their promises.',119782,119800),(6543,8,'Secondly, they are the powerful figures who can come out persuasively and urge people to tamp down.',119801,119817),(6544,8,'But thirdly, the protests are more willing to negotiate with them when they\'re in government, because they have a history of being receptive to protest, rather than turning to violence because they feel like the government will never listen, because protests will never work.',119818,119861),(6545,8,'That was good.',119862,119864),(6546,8,'I thank the speaker very much for this speech.',119865,119873),(6547,8,'Now I\'d like to give the government whip to follow up government venture.',119874,119886),(6548,8,'First, I\'ll explain why closing the government wins the debate, and secondly, why the Opposition bench loses.',119887,119903),(6549,8,'Firstly, why did we win the debate?',119904,119910),(6550,8,'I think we made kind of two contributions.',119911,119918),(6551,8,'The first is just explaining in substantial detail why these student leaders would be both bad at politics, but also, perhaps more importantly, good at civil society, and impacting why that is a society and politics changing force.',119919,119956),(6552,8,'And the second, I think, is just outlining that most of these specific demands of the anti-discrimination student movement, in their highly publicised 9.',119957,119981),(6553,8,'0 plan, published after closing the scene up, are bad.',119982,119991),(6554,8,'And of course, as this team might respond, some of those demands are like, for instance, asking for compensation for families who have protested to a hill. That\'s fine.',119992,120020),(6555,8,'But those kind of demands are not sensationalist, nor are they radical.',120021,120032),(6556,8,'They\'re extremely unlikely to be the focus of campaigns, of opposition, of media, of the things that they are held to by political opponents, and that are indeed the spotlight for the media at the moment.',120033,120068),(6557,8,'Many of those demands are incredibly bad.',120069,120075),(6558,8,'Things like firing huge tracks of police who are related to the university.',120076,120088),(6559,8,'or whose jurisdiction is the universities where protest was suppressed, even if those police were not directly involved, like they didn\'t kill a person, they just have jurisdiction over those universities, no security at the universities, firing fuse attacks at VCs, and national boundary alarming the uni-quake.',120089,120136),(6560,8,'And I think those policies are bad in a few respects.',120137,120147),(6561,8,'Firstly, I don\'t suppose many of them on face value on their grounds alone.',120148,120161),(6562,8,'For instance, I don\'t think you should ban student movements of most political parties until they pass a minimum and extremely high threshold.',120162,120184),(6563,8,'I think that is probably something we should be conservative about, not restricting free speech.',120185,120199),(6564,8,'I think police who are often underpaid, who are not personally responsible for violence against students, who happen to be part of a systemically corrupt institution, but don\'t have much choice in that, should not be fired from their jobs.',120200,120239),(6565,8,'I think those are immoral demands and we should not stand for them.',120240,120252),(6566,8,'Secondly, those demands are literally impossible to fulfil.',120253,120260),(6567,8,'As Ellie points out to No Response, without powerful enemies in the form of the whole police force, this is incredibly scary.',120261,120282),(6568,8,'This doesn\'t work, which at very worst for us, which is an enormous opportunity cost of resources, a failure to get your policies passed.',120283,120306),(6569,8,'But also I think it\'s incredibly embarrassing and delegitimising for these student protests and for all the civil society organisations and movements that we\'ve heard that they\'re attached to, when they can do good work out of politics.',120307,120344),(6570,8,'Maybe, for instance, you want to go into politics later, you can\'t because you have an initial track record of doing terrible things and failing to pass through a policy.',120345,120374),(6571,8,'The response we get to this from opening opposition in a POI is, firstly, well if there\'s a risk of coup, then you moderate.',120375,120398),(6572,8,'I think Ellie pre-empts this in quite a lot of detail.',120399,120410),(6573,8,'We explain people aren\'t rational, that it\'s very unlikely that there\'s a risk of a coup on their side, and you\'re not thinking about the future to that extent.',120411,120439),(6574,8,'But it\'s incredibly embarrassing and maybe, for instance, brings backlash or political violence in the short term to backtrack on your established demands.',120440,120462),(6575,8,'And importantly, even if some people are rational in this way, the most prominent leaders of that movement will not be.',120463,120483),(6576,8,'The second plan they made is, well if you don\'t moderate, you\'re going to lose the election.',120484,120500),(6577,8,'But firstly, I don\'t know if that harms the movement of anti-authoritarian student protesters.',120501,120515),(6578,8,'Regardless, even if it\'s true that you lose the election by having these demands, it still hurts that movement.',120516,120534),(6579,8,'It hurts, for instance, initial movements by students, any student in Bangladesh against corruption, against authoritarianism in the future.',120535,120553),(6580,8,'They are targeted that brush.',120554,120558),(6581,8,'It\'s really idiotic for opposition parties to media outlets to pick up on.',120559,120571),(6582,8,'But secondly, maybe at their very best, this plan hurts OG, because we explain our why involved in civil society.',120572,120591),(6583,8,'Successfully put politics later, for instance.',120592,120597),(6584,8,'And you could run more successfully put politics later, if you\'re not targeted this brush.',120598,120612),(6585,8,'If, for instance, you have demands that are bad, that can\'t operate in civil society, probably still do with.',120613,120631),(6586,8,'And in politics, in representing this constituency in parliament, you cause huge amounts of chaos.',120632,120646),(6587,8,'You shift the Overton window.',120647,120651),(6588,8,'You mean that people discredit other, more sensible left-wing policies, like restrictions on police powers.',120652,120667),(6589,8,'You mean that there\'s gridlock in parliament.',120668,120674),(6590,8,'All of that is terrible.',120675,120679),(6591,8,'Why does this then get us above opening government?',120680,120688),(6592,8,'I take a fairly generic criticism of young left revolutionaries on the basis of their radicalism, but also the tempting vices of politics like corruption.',120689,120713),(6593,8,'But the problem with this is, firstly, claims in terms of entitlement to corruption, while true, I think seem relatively symmetric, given the features that this team themselves point out in terms of the political system in Bangladesh at large.',120714,120753),(6594,8,'But secondly, radicalism, of course, and our opening text, hand you back, but can also be put, right, at deeply radical movements, like, for instance, anti-caste movements or feminism, are both good ideologically, but are deeply attractive to people, even though they ask for very large changes to the status quo.',120754,120805),(6595,8,'We explain that the changes we\'re asking for are bad, which means they\'re both unpopular, but also undesirable.',120806,120823),(6596,8,'But finally, we impact the alternative.',120824,120829),(6597,8,'Civil society, not just politics, which makes society and makes government better. We win.',120830,120843),(6598,8,'Let\'s now talk about opening opposition.',120844,120849),(6599,8,'Opening opposition, I think, is dangerously pessimistic in their vision of the status quo.',120850,120863),(6600,8,'They say that the NDP will have no political competition without students to push back.',120864,120878),(6601,8,'The reason for this is because it\'s prohibitively hard for the youth to vote, the BNP receives money from lobbyists, they\'ll always get young people on side, students don\'t win.',120879,120908),(6602,8,'This is dangerous because it\'s a self-defeating argument for opening opposition.',120909,120920),(6603,8,'If the BNP is so powerful, then students collecting and testing elections will fail regardless.',120921,120935),(6604,8,'And their one attempt to bridge this gap is to say, well, people care a lot about youth and revolution now, we have to take that opportunity.',120936,120962),(6605,8,'That isn\'t sufficient for a few reasons.',120963,120969),(6606,8,'Firstly, it could lose that momentum, right?',120970,120976),(6607,8,'Like, if you present yourself as political critics, part of civil society, it is likely that anti-authoritarian 